# Where Are We — live project board

This project has a live visual flowchart the user keeps open. You keep it current by
editing exactly one file: `data/where-are-we.json`. Edits appear on the canvas within a
moment, sketched in by hand. Read `data/NEXT.md` for the current next move after a
context reset. Full details in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).

## When to update the board

- **New milestone** → add a `project` node with a `section` and `blockedBy`
  (prerequisite ids). These drive the flowchart, gold critical path, and the
  "Do this next" banner — be accurate about dependencies.
- **Progress** → update `status` (`todo` → `doing` → `done`) and bump `updatedAt`.
- **Each work session** → add `daily` nodes with today's `day` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), a
  `section`, and `projectRef` pointing at the project node they advanced.
- **Flow** → add `edges` between project nodes (they also count as dependencies).

## Use graphify for accurate edges

Before writing `link` fields, `edges`, or `blockedBy`, run `graphify query "<question>"`
or `graphify path "A" "B"` against `graphify-out/graph.json` so declared dependencies
reflect how the code actually connects. Run `graphify update .` after code changes.

## Rules

- Only edit `data/where-are-we.json`. **Never** `data/layout.local.json` (the user's
  layout + personal edits) or `data/NEXT.md` (generated).
- Keep node `id`s **stable and unique**; reuse the same id when updating a thing.
- Always write valid JSON (read → modify → write the whole file).
- Never set colors; color derives from `status`, gold highlighting is automatic.
- Bump `updatedAt` on meaningful change (re-triggers the draw-in animation).
- Card copy is sticky-note sized: `title` ≤ ~6 words, `note` one short line (the card
  clamps the title at 3 lines and the note at 4 — long text is simply lost).
- Titles must be readable cold, by a human, weeks later. No invented internal nouns
  ("pause-on-post hard rail"), no flag names (`META_LIVE`), no unexplained acronyms —
  say what it does ("Ads always start paused"). Mechanism belongs in the note.

## Shapes

```jsonc
// section:  { "id": "sec-x", "title": "Backend", "order": 1 }
// project:  { "id": "proj-x", "title": "...", "status": "todo|doing|done", "note": "...",
//             "view": "project", "section": "sec-x", "blockedBy": ["proj-y"],
//             "link": { "file": "src/x.ts", "line": 10 }, "createdAt": ISO, "updatedAt": ISO }
// daily:    { "id": "day-...", "title": "...", "status": "done", "view": "daily",
//             "day": "YYYY-MM-DD", "section": "sec-x", "projectRef": "proj-x",
//             "createdAt": ISO, "updatedAt": ISO }
// edge:     { "id": "e-x-y", "from": "proj-x", "to": "proj-y", "label": "optional" }
```
